Task 3: Add Panels with Visualizations
Subtask 3.1: Create a Graph Panel for CPU Usage
Create your first visualization panel:

Click Add panel and select Add new panel
In the Query section:
Select Prometheus as data source
Enter this query: 100 - (avg(irate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode="idle"}[5m])) * 100)
Set Legend: CPU Usage %
In the Panel section:
Title: CPU Usage Over Time
Description: Shows CPU utilization percentage over time
In the Visualization section:
Select Time series (graph)
Configure Graph styles:
Style: Line
Line width: 2
Fill opacity: 10
In the Field section:
Unit: Percent (0-100)
Min: 0
Max: 100
Click Apply to save the panel
Subtask 3.2: Create a Table Panel for System Information
Add a table visualization:

Click Add panel and select Add new panel
In the Query section, add multiple queries:
Query A: node_uname_info
Query B: node_boot_time_seconds
Query C: node_load1
Query D: node_load5
Query E: node_load15
In the Panel section:
Title: System Information
Description: Key system metrics and information
In the Visualization section:
Select Table
Configure table columns:
Click Field tab
Add Override for each field to customize display names
Click Apply to save the panel
Subtask 3.3: Create Gauge Panels for Key Metrics
Create gauge visualizations for important metrics:

Memory Usage Gauge
Click Add panel and select Add new panel
In the Query section:
Query: (1 - (node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes / node_memory_MemTotal_bytes)) * 100
Legend: Memory Usage
In the Panel section:
Title: Memory Usage
Description: Current memory utilization
In the Visualization section:
Select Gauge
Configure gauge settings:
Min: 0
Max: 100
Unit: Percent (0-100)
In the Thresholds section:
Green: 0-70
Yellow: 70-85
Red: 85-100
Click Apply to save
Disk Usage Gauge
Click Add panel and select Add new panel
In the Query section:
Query: (1 - (node_filesystem_avail_bytes{mountpoint="/"} / node_filesystem_size_bytes{mountpoint="/"})) * 100
Legend: Disk Usage
In the Panel section:
Title: Root Disk Usage
Description: Root filesystem utilization
In the Visualization section:
Select Gauge
Configure similar to memory gauge
Set appropriate thresholds for disk usage
Click Apply to save
Network Traffic Gauge
Click Add panel and select Add new panel
In the Query section:
Query A: irate(node_network_receive_bytes_total{device!="lo"}[5m]) * 8
Query B: irate(node_network_transmit_bytes_total{device!="lo"}[5m]) * 8
In the Panel section:
Title: Network Traffic
Description: Network receive and transmit rates
In the Visualization section:
Select Stat or Gauge
Unit: bits/sec
Click Apply to save
